From: Stefano Viola <stefano.viola@toradex.com>
Subject: [PATCH] adbd: use /tmp as TMPDIR when /data/local/tmp is missing

adb shells get TMPDIR=/data/local/tmp, which only exists on Android. On a
Linux distribution tools run through adb (e.g. arduino-app-cli, which App
Lab drives over adb) fail creating temporary files. Fall back to /tmp.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Stefano Viola <stefano.viola@toradex.com>
---
--- a/packages/modules/adb/daemon/shell_service.cpp
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/daemon/shell_service.cpp
@@ -274,7 +274,8 @@
         env["HOSTNAME"] = GetHostName();
         env["LOGNAME"] = pw->pw_name;
         env["SHELL"] = pw->pw_shell;
-        env["TMPDIR"] = "/data/local/tmp";
+        // Android's /data/local/tmp does not exist on Linux distributions
+        env["TMPDIR"] = access("/data/local/tmp", F_OK) == 0 ? "/data/local/tmp" : "/tmp";
         env["USER"] = pw->pw_name;
     }
 
